My honest reaction?

This is the strongest answer the LRM has produced so far, but I still would not approve it yet.

The reason is not that it's a bad idea. It is actually intelligent and much closer to the value hidden in your data.

The problem is that I think it is still trying to answer:

"What intervention works?"

when the data you have is probably much better suited to answering:

"What is the bank repeatedly learning and re-learning?"

Those sound similar, but they are very different.

